A||N||6||87FieroGT||Rollin on new wheels!!!||||6
Z||000000||87FieroGT||10-12-1999||10:51 PM||||Well I thought I might share some rim and wheel info to everyone. Just got my new rims and rubber today at Discount Tire. I went with some 16" Konig Rush Rims surrounded by Interceptor 245/45/ZR 16's. The guy at the store did all the math and these size tire combination are the same radius as the original 195/60/15's. The tires look very good on my ride and are very wide. If anyone was wondering how much it all costs it came in at a little over $1,100 dollars. I didn't think it was to bad of a deal. Anyway I am now a happy camper.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Terrybogin||10-12-1999||11:12 PM||||Wow! Your wheels and tires costs as much as my car. But a good set of wheels can really make a car look nice. Like a Pinto- a set of wheels and you have got a cool ride! Well, maybe not, but it helps!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Shiner||10-13-1999||03:22 AM||||I'd really like to see some pics of those on your car.  Do you have any?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||10-13-1999||07:58 AM||||I would love to see pictures, too. I've been thinking about doing the same thing and was wondering about the max tire width and rim offsets. The one thing I don't want in for the tires and wheels to stick out beyong the fender... never liked the roller skate look.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000004||87FieroGT||10-13-1999||10:27 PM||||I will try to get some pics up on the forum if can ever find enough time to take the pictures and then actually take them to get developed. I may do it this weekend and get it done on the new CD-Rom feature so that I don't have to bother with a scanner.||||reg||10
Z||000005||87GTBro||10-16-1999||10:21 PM||||I don't want to steal any of his glory, but 87FieroGT 's car looks great!<BR>In case there is confusion, I am his brother.  The rims look great!  It is nice riding with him and watching all the heads turn when we pass by.  <BR>Today, we drove out to South Padre Island to do some sea kayaking.  Also going on at the island today was a Harley Davidson bike show called Roar By the Shore.  We cruised up and down the strip with the bikers and got a lot of looks.<BR>While stopped on the side of the street to watch the parade, some bikers with nice Harley's pulled up next to us and we talked for a while.  Right before leaving, one made the comment, "I believe that is one of the nicest Fieros I have seen."  I'm sure that was an ego booster.<BR>Hopefully soon, I will join in with an '87 GT of my own.  Currently looking into a red one to join with my brother's blue one.  <BR>Wish me luck!||||reg||14
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||10-17-1999||04:10 AM||||Hiya 87GTBro, and welcome to the club!<P>I've been looking for a nice set of 16" rims for a long time now, but haven't found anything I liked yet. I've got factory 15" spoke-rims now and actually all I want are the same (or similar) ones but in 16".||||reg||1
